# Line endings
#
# The team develops on Windows, macOS and Linux, so endings must not depend
# on whoever last touched a file. `.gitattributes` is the cross-platform
# source of truth for this: unlike core.autocrlf (a per-machine setting that
# every clone has to remember to set) it travels with the repository.
#
# Default: text files are normalised to LF on check-in.
* text=auto

# POSIX scripts and CI definitions MUST stay LF on every platform — a single
# CRLF in a shell script makes the shebang line `#!/bin/sh^M`, which CI and
# macOS/Linux shells reject outright. Pinning eol=lf here overrides the
# Windows checkout conversion for exactly these paths.
*.sh text eol=lf
scripts/git-hooks/* text eol=lf
.github/workflows/*.yml text eol=lf
Taskfile.yml text eol=lf

# Generated Wails bindings are regenerated by the Go toolchain on every
# `wails3 generate bindings`; keeping them LF avoids churn between hosts.
frontend/bindings/** text eol=lf

# Lockstep with the binaries below: these are data, never text-diffed.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.syso binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
